    <item>
      <title>C# Basics</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/7270-NguyenVietAnh/7270-NguyenVietAnh/posts/csharp-basics/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 27 Dec 2024 10:00:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/7270-NguyenVietAnh/7270-NguyenVietAnh/posts/csharp-basics/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;introduction-to-c&#34;&gt;Introduction to C#&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;C# is a modern, powerful, and object-oriented programming language developed by Microsoft. It is widely used for developing desktop applications, web applications, games, and cloud services.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;features-of-c&#34;&gt;Features of C#&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object-Oriented&lt;/strong&gt;: C# fully supports object-oriented programming with classes, inheritance, polymorphism, and encapsulation.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Type-Safe&lt;/strong&gt;: C# is a strongly typed language, preventing many common programming errors.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Garbage Collection&lt;/strong&gt;: Automatic memory management through garbage collection.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rich Framework&lt;/strong&gt;: .NET Framework provides extensive libraries for various development tasks.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Platform&lt;/strong&gt;: With .NET Core and .NET 5+, C# can run on Windows, Linux, and macOS.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;basic-structure-of-a-c-program&#34;&gt;Basic Structure of a C# Program&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Below is a simple C# program:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>C# Object-Oriented Programming</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/7270-NguyenVietAnh/7270-NguyenVietAnh/posts/csharp-oop/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 27 Dec 2024 11:00:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/7270-NguyenVietAnh/7270-NguyenVietAnh/posts/csharp-oop/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;c-object-oriented-programming&#34;&gt;C# Object-Oriented Programming&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) is a fundamental concept in C#. It helps organize code into logical units called classes and objects, making programs more maintainable and scalable.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;core-oop-principles&#34;&gt;Core OOP Principles&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;1-encapsulation&#34;&gt;1. Encapsulation&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Encapsulation involves bundling data (properties) and methods (behaviors) into a single unit (class) and hiding the internal details.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-csharp&#34; data-lang=&#34;csharp&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Person&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; name;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; age;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; GetName() {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; name;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; SetName(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; n) {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        name = n;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;2-inheritance&#34;&gt;2. Inheritance&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Inheritance allows a class to inherit properties and methods from a parent class.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Asynchronous Programming in C#</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/7270-NguyenVietAnh/7270-NguyenVietAnh/posts/csharp-async/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 27 Dec 2024 12:00:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/7270-NguyenVietAnh/7270-NguyenVietAnh/posts/csharp-async/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;asynchronous-programming-in-c&#34;&gt;Asynchronous Programming in C#&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Asynchronous programming allows long-running operations to be executed without blocking the main thread. In C#, this is achieved using &lt;code&gt;async&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;await&lt;/code&gt; keywords.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;understanding-tasks&#34;&gt;Understanding Tasks&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A &lt;code&gt;Task&lt;/code&gt; represents an asynchronous operation that will complete in the future.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-csharp&#34; data-lang=&#34;csharp&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Task&amp;lt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt; CalculateAsync() {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; Task.FromResult(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;42&lt;/span&gt;);&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;asyncawait-pattern&#34;&gt;Async/Await Pattern&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;async&lt;/code&gt; keyword marks a method as asynchronous, and &lt;code&gt;await&lt;/code&gt; pauses execution until the Task completes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-csharp&#34; data-lang=&#34;csharp&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; Task FetchDataAsync() {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; response = &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; GetDataFromServer();&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        Console.WriteLine(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Data: &amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; + response);&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    } &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt; (Exception ex) {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        Console.WriteLine(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Error: &amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; + ex.Message);&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; Task&amp;lt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt; GetDataFromServer() {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; Task.Delay(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1000&lt;/span&gt;);&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Server Data&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;parallel-execution-with-taskwhenall&#34;&gt;Parallel Execution with Task.WhenAll&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Execute multiple asynchronous operations concurrently.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>LINQ in C#</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/7270-NguyenVietAnh/7270-NguyenVietAnh/posts/csharp-linq/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 27 Dec 2024 13:00:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/7270-NguyenVietAnh/7270-NguyenVietAnh/posts/csharp-linq/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;linq-in-c&#34;&gt;LINQ in C#&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;LINQ (Language Integrated Query) is a powerful feature in C# that allows you to query and manipulate data from various sources using a consistent syntax.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-is-linq&#34;&gt;What is LINQ?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;LINQ provides a uniform way to query data from different sources such as arrays, lists, databases, and XML documents.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;linq-query-syntax&#34;&gt;LINQ Query Syntax&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;basic-query&#34;&gt;Basic Query:&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-csharp&#34; data-lang=&#34;csharp&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;using&lt;/span&gt; System;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;using&lt;/span&gt; System.Linq;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;[] numbers = { &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;5&lt;/span&gt; };&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; result = &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; num &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; numbers&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;             &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;where&lt;/span&gt; num &amp;gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;             &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;select&lt;/span&gt; num;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;foreach&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; item &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; result) {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    Console.WriteLine(item);&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// Output: 3, 4, 5&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;linq-method-syntax&#34;&gt;LINQ Method Syntax&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Method syntax is more flexible and allows chaining of operations.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
